>> title: Grandma Pie
>> category: Pizzas
>> tags: pizza, tomato, mozzarella, square, italian, oven
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: grandma, grandma pie, grandma square, grandma slice, grandma style, grandma pizza, nonna pizza
>> pairs-with: pizza-dough
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 30 min

Preheat the #oven{} to 500°F (260°C) with a rack in the lowest slot ~preheat{45%min}.

>> step: press cold dough into an oiled sheet, twice
Press @pizza dough{2%balls}(250 g each, cold from the fridge; from the recipe on this shelf) into a #half-sheet pan{} slicked with @extra-virgin olive oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL), ~rest{30%min} when it starts pulling back, then press it out again to the corners.

>> step: crush raw, garlic straight in
Crush @whole peeled tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g; drained) with @garlic{2%cloves}(grated), @dried oregano{1%tsp} and @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}, and leave it raw.

>> step: scatter the cheese, dollop the tomato
Scatter @low-moisture mozzarella{8%oz}(225 g; cut in 1/2-in cubes) over @&(~2)pressed dough{}, then dollop @&(~1)crushed tomato{} over the cheese in spoonfuls, leaving bare patches between them.

>> step: bake 500°F (260°C) 16 to 20 min
Bake @&(~1)pie{} on the low rack ~bake{18%min}, until the cheese along the edge has fried dark against the pan and the dough underneath is crisp all the way to the middle.

>> step: finish with pecorino, basil and oil
Finish @&(~1)grandma pie{} with @grated pecorino{1/4%cup}(25 g), @fresh basil{8%leaves} and @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL).

The dough is pressed out cold with no second proof. The tomato goes on raw and in dollops so it roasts in patches.
